 "notes": "Papercut (jianzhi) rabbit, final. One continuous white silhouette in wrapper-blue line: head, body, tail, near hind leg and near foreleg are a single closed contour; both ears are back layers whose roots tuck behind the skull, so the head line passes cleanly over them, and they open into a V with a clear slot above the back; the inner ear is pink, drawn before the body so the head covers its root. Interior cuts: one haunch spiral (about one turn, open centre) and a small shoulder comma. Red eye with a front-top glint, pink nose pad set inside the profile. Leap: nose up 3 degrees, one hind leg trailing on a diagonal with a heel break and a rounded toe, one foreleg reaching with an oval paw (the far legs are tucked out of sight, so there is no fork or double line at icon sizes); lowest point y 149.5. Gather (resting/landing pose): a coiled crouch on its toes: round haunch, heel raised, the hind foot sloping to a short contact strip on y = 150, an ankle notch and knee, a near-vertical forearm with the paw forward. Stretch: the leap's body with the hind leg pushed back and the foreleg reaching forward. Morph: the hind foot slides instead of turning (stretch toe = gather heel, stretch underside = gather sole), so the foot keeps 92 to 100 percent of its outline length at every t and the rear x falls steadily; nothing crosses itself in any pose or in-between. Layers: back far ear, back near ear, pink inner ear, back far foreleg, main, line haunch spiral, line shoulder comma, red eye, white glint, pink nose. Stroke weights: W 5 at 300 px and up, 6 at 120 px, 9 to 11 at 28 to 48 px; the line layers read best lighter at small sizes (about 5 for the 38 px header, 4 to 4.5 for the band and 60 px icons, 0 for the 28 to 32 px nested icons)."
